release_secrets.txt

# Research-round working corpus (2026-09 engineering-canon round). Bulk source
# material and scratch notes that live in the working tree but must never enter
# git history: `books/` alone is ~1.1 GB of third-party PDFs, and an accidental
# `git add -A` would commit a copyrighted corpus to a public repo. The durable
# outputs of that round are folded into docs/ as normal tracked pages.
/books/
/_extracts/
/research-round-charter.md
/maidan_engineering_knowledge_base_github.md
/maidan_engineering_knowledge_base_post_first_download_set.md
/maidan_kb_processing_prompt.md
/maidan_world_launch_design_reference_catalog.md
# Per-agent scratch notes staged under docs/ (underscore-prefixed by convention).
docs/_*

# The 2026-09 research round's working notes. Untracked *and* unignored, they
# have twice been swept into a commit by a `git add -A docs/` — once far enough
# to reach a remote branch. Ignoring them decides nothing about whether they
# eventually belong in the repo: `git add -f` still stages any of them
# deliberately. It only removes the accident.
/docs/research-*.md
/docs/reddit-mine-*.md
/docs/Baked.md
/docs/Book Roadmap.md
/docs/Fabrics.md
/docs/Fold Ready.md
/docs/Gaps.md
/docs/GitHub Roadmap.md
/docs/Horizon.md
/docs/Industry.md
/docs/Integration Reality.md
/docs/Launch Roadmap.md
/docs/Massive Roadmap.md
/docs/Missed.md
/docs/Propose.md
/docs/Reddit Gems.md
/docs/Source Map.md
/docs/Splice Prompt.md
/docs/Undeniable.md
/docs/Undeniable Final.md

# External audit working corpus — reference material, not repo content.
/maidan-audit-corpus/
/maidan-docs-audit-corpus/
